!THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md

# Handicraft additions.
# These are local build output and runtime state. They must never enter the
# image: the Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything listed here would be baked
# into the published layers. handicraft-local.db in particular contains real
# account data (usernames and bcrypt password hashes), and the two binaries are
# >120 MB each, which inflates the build context sent to the Docker daemon.
handicraft-*
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
logs

# Host-side compose secrets. docker compose reads .env for variable
# substitution; it is never needed inside the build context, and `COPY . .`
# would otherwise pull the Postgres and Redis passwords into a builder layer.
.env
.env.*
